&lt;p&gt;Do you follow every shift in digital marketing, media and commerce, and always have a view on which stories matter the most?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do you want to create content across channels that educates the next generation of marketers?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Does the idea of shaping the content for one of digital marketing&#39;s longest-running publications excite you?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If so, we&#39;d love to hear from you!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fospha is the measurement system enterprise retail and ecommerce brands run their business on. We give marketing teams one clear, daily view of what&#39;s actually working — across every channel and everywhere they sell, from their website to Amazon and TikTok Shop — down to the level of a single ad or piece of creative. It replaces guesswork and gut feel with a number marketing, finance and agencies can all trust and act on. Brands including Dyson, Gymshark, and Lululemon use Fospha up to 25 times a day to decide where budget should move next. We&#39;ve spent over a decade building this, with more than $40 billion in marketing spend now optimised through the platform — and we&#39;re scaling fast across London, Mumbai and Austin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About ClickZ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://clickz.com/&quot;&gt;ClickZ&lt;/a&gt; is Fospha&#39;s media partner and one of the world&#39;s longest-running digital marketing publications, trusted by CMOs and senior marketers since 1997. Its focus is how measurement shapes marketing decisions, and it covers the wider marketing that measurement informs. Readers come to ClickZ to understand:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How marketing leaders build teams, explain results to finance and earn influence in the room&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retail and commerce marketing, including retail media and marketplaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How AI, search and ad platform changes affect planning and results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Where to invest across brand, creative, performance, affiliate and influencer marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How brands measure performance, from attribution and incrementality to mix modelling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a permanent role at the heart of ClickZ. You&#39;ll run the day-to-day content engine: spotting the stories that matter to marketing leaders, turning them into sharp content across email, social and the website, and growing the audience that reads it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The work is varied. In a single week you might cover a session at a major commerce event, publish a piece on a platform change, prepare a leadership Q&amp;amp;A, and review a stack of contributor pitches. You&#39;ll also build ClickZ&#39;s network of event partners, contributors, PR contacts and industry leaders, and meet many of them in person at industry events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with ClickZ&#39;s lead, who sets the brand&#39;s strategy, and you&#39;ll have real ownership of your workstreams from the start. This is an &lt;strong&gt;office-based role&lt;/strong&gt; in London.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role suits someone with a journalist&#39;s instinct for a story, a marketer&#39;s eye for an audience, and the energy to keep both going every week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll work on&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your time will be spread across three areas, with content creation at the core. All three serve one goal: growing the ClickZ brand and getting its content to more of the right people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Focus area&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What it covers&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Content creation&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The core of the role: editorial content on market trends, event coverage, brand leadership interviews and Q&amp;amp;As, flagship newsletters, and social content&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Audience growth and content analysis&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Growing ClickZ&#39;s readership and subscribers, testing new formats, and using performance data to decide what to create next&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Network and community&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Building relationships with event partners, marketing and commerce leaders, PR teams and contributors, online and in person at industry events&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep the content engine fed.&lt;/strong&gt; Track the news and trends that matter to marketing and commerce leaders, and turn them into timely, well-argued content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the bar on every channel.&lt;/strong&gt; Bring a creative eye to email, social and web content, and build a distinct content plan for each channel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the flagship newsletters.&lt;/strong&gt; Draft and refine ClickZ&#39;s flagship newsletters, and develop more tailored formats for different parts of the audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring leadership conversations to life.&lt;/strong&gt; Prepare and support podcast and Q&amp;amp;A conversations with leaders across marketing and commerce, and, with training and support, grow into hosting them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow the audience.&lt;/strong&gt; Work out which formats and topics readers respond to, and turn readers into subscribers. Design campaigns that bring back readers who&#39;ve gone quiet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Let data inform the calls.&lt;/strong&gt; Track what content delivers, use the numbers to decide what to do next, and share what&#39;s working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the first filter.&lt;/strong&gt; Review PR pitches and contributor submissions, and pick out the strong and relevant ones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the network.&lt;/strong&gt; Reach out to contributors, speakers and event partners, grow an always-on contributor community, and build lasting relationships with PR teams and industry leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get out into the industry.&lt;/strong&gt; Attend events, support event partnerships, and find new events worth ClickZ&#39;s time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work agentically.&lt;/strong&gt; Use AI tools to speed up research, drafting and multimedia content, while owning the quality of what goes out.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What are we looking for?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We hire for potential and taste. You should apply if you meet these six must-haves:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have around one year of experience creating content in the digital marketing, media or commerce world, whether in journalism, editorial, content or social roles (internships, placements and personal projects count), and a genuine passion for digital marketing and commerce, and for the leaders shaping them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have &lt;strong&gt;strong editorial judgement&lt;/strong&gt;: you can tell good content from weak, and relevant from noise, and you know a big story when you see one (experience of writing, editing or curating, including student or personal publications)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a &lt;strong&gt;creative eye to content&lt;/strong&gt; across email, social and web, with a feel for multimedia formats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are &lt;strong&gt;audience-minded&lt;/strong&gt;: you think about who&#39;s reading, how to reach more of the right people and how to build a community around a brand. You&#39;re also comfortable with data: you use performance numbers to make content decisions and back up your conclusions (experience using analytics such as GA4)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are &lt;strong&gt;agentically minded&lt;/strong&gt;: you love experimenting with new tools for multimedia content creation and adaptation, and know when to push them and when to take over&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are &lt;strong&gt;a natural conversationalist&lt;/strong&gt;: you get a guest talking, hold your own with senior leaders, and leave an event with new connections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Also important:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have &lt;strong&gt;high agency&lt;/strong&gt;: you take ownership of your work, stretch beyond the brief and challenge the status quo when something could be better&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy a fast-paced, innovative startup environment, where you&#39;ll ship quickly, iterate often and juggle several projects at once&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are happy to travel for industry events, within the UK and occasionally overseas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Values and Principles&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be able to demonstrate examples of our core principles:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seek inclusion &amp;amp; diversity:&lt;/strong&gt; We create an environment where everyone feels welcome, and people are encouraged to speak and be heard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Hard, Work Well, Work Together:&lt;/strong&gt; We take responsibility for making things happen, independently and together; we help colleagues in need and close loops, making sure our work is complete and has lasting impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow:&lt;/strong&gt; We are proactive, curious and unafraid of failure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer at the heart:&lt;/strong&gt; We care about the customer, feel their pain and love building product that solves their biggest problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candour with caring:&lt;/strong&gt; We deliver candid feedback with kindness and receive it with gratitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we can offer you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary: £34k + discretionary 10% bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership of content for a media brand that has covered digital marketing for nearly 30 years&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Early ownership of your workstreams, and the chance to shape how modern marketers learn and make decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A growing network across PR teams, contributors and industry leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on podcast experience, with regular conversations with leaders across marketing and commerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A place at major industry events, with a front-row view of commerce, media and digital marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be part of a leading global venture builder, &lt;a href=&quot;https://blenheimchalcot.com/blog&quot;&gt;Blenheim Chalcot&lt;/a&gt;, and learn from the incredible talent in BC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The right mix of challenges, learning and development opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A workplace pension, through Royal London, with Fospha matching your contributions up to 3%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A £1,000/year flexible benefits allowance to put towards private medical insurance, dental cover, a health cash plan, gym membership, extra holiday, or a pension top-up - whatever suits you!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to Wellhub, giving you one membership across gyms, boutique studios, and wellbeing apps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days&#39; annual leave plus 8 UK bank holidays, an extra day off for your birthday! and more holiday the longer you stay (26 days after 3 years, 27 after 6)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life assurance worth 4x your annual salary, from day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cycle to Work scheme, plus discounts on everyday spending through our benefits portal — Apple, Tesco, IKEA, M&amp;amp;S, Deliveroo, cinema tickets and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quarterly one-to-one sessions with a financial adviser, plus access to payroll-deducted loans through Salary Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid volunteering days each year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular socials, free weekly snacks, and Lunch &amp;amp; Learn events at our Scale Space office, plus access to the wider Blenheim Chalcot community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities to travel — including to our India and North America offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Top tip: Share two or three pieces of content you&#39;re proud of, and tell us one story ClickZ should cover next, and why.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Fospha&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fospha is the measurement system enterprise retail and ecommerce brands run their business on. We give marketing teams one clear, daily view of what&#39;s actually working - across every channel and everywhere they sell, from their website to Amazon and TikTok Shop - down to the level of a single ad or piece of creative. It replaces guesswork and gut feel with a number marketing, finance and agencies can all trust and act on. Brands including Dyson, Gymshark, and Lululemon use Fospha every day to decide where budget should move next. We&#39;ve spent over a decade building this, with more than $40 billion in marketing spend now optimised through the platform - and we&#39;re scaling fast across London, Mumbai and Austin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring two Product Managers to own major parts of the Fospha platform. You&#39;ll decide what gets built and why, get it shipped, and prove it worked for clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for a doer. You&#39;ll own a significant product area end to end, set its direction, and run several initiatives at once. A delivery manager and engineering lead run day-to-day delivery alongside you, so your time goes on the decisions that matter: which client problem to solve, what it&#39;s worth, what to cut, and whether what shipped actually moved the needle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join an established team, supporting our continued transformation in a post-AI era. We&#39;re looking for people who will push how we structure and execute to maximise the value of Product work, not take their first step into Product management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own a product area end to end.&lt;/strong&gt; Take initiatives from problem, sizing and discovery through build, launch and adoption. Make the sequencing calls for your area and run several initiatives in parallel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start every initiative with why.&lt;/strong&gt; Before anything is built, be clear on the client problem, the evidence for it, the expected impact for clients, what it&#39;s worth commercially, how it fits our pricing and packaging, and how it advances company strategy. Fospha&#39;s business strategy hinges on its product strategy, so every initiative should trace back to it. Say no to good ideas that aren&#39;t the most important thing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay close to clients.&lt;/strong&gt; Don&#39;t wait to be invited: set up your own client calls as well as joining others&#39;, run interviews and prototype sessions, and pair what clients tell you with what the usage data shows. Know what clients see on screen and what they do with it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decide quickly on imperfect information.&lt;/strong&gt; Know when the evidence is strong enough to act, make the call, and change course when the evidence changes, including stopping work that isn&#39;t landing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work AI-first.&lt;/strong&gt; Use AI to compress discovery synthesis, analysis, spec writing and stakeholder communication. Build and refine your own agents, workflows and prototypes, and work with engineers on what can be prototyped with AI coding tools. Share what works with other PMs and feed improvements back to Product Ops, so the whole team gets faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prove it worked.&lt;/strong&gt; Set success thresholds before build starts, check adoption and usage after release, and act on the result. Shipped is not the same as worked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Give people what they need to decide.&lt;/strong&gt; Know what information a decision-maker needs at each point, and give them exactly that: a one-line recommendation for an exec, the full detail for an engineer. Present with confidence to senior leaders, internally and at clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the bar.&lt;/strong&gt; Give direct, useful feedback, take it well, and hold your own work to a high standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll bring (must-haves)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3+ years as a Product Manager, or in an adjacent role with experience you can clearly apply to product management.&lt;/strong&gt; Either way, you can point to problems you owned end to end: deciding what to do, getting it delivered, and measuring whether it worked against success criteria set upfront.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2+ years making decisions from data yourself&lt;/strong&gt; - product analytics (funnels, usage, retention) and commercial data - pulling and checking your own numbers rather than waiting for an analyst.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A track record of connecting your work to commercial outcomes.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve sized opportunities in revenue or retention terms, built business cases, and shaped pricing, packaging or monetisation decisions with commercial teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on client experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve run customer discovery, joined sales and account calls, and turned what clients experience into a clear, evidenced problem statement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Confidence in presenting to peers and senior stakeholders.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;re confident making and presenting recommendations to leaders across the business, advocating for data-backed decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep, everyday use of AI in your work.&lt;/strong&gt; You can describe specific workflows, agents or tools you&#39;ve built or configured, the work they replaced, and how you check their output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How you work&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conscientious.&lt;/strong&gt; You close loops, follow through on what you said you&#39;d do, and catch data or quality issues before they reach a client.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relentless about prioritisation.&lt;/strong&gt; You can explain why this, why now and what it&#39;s worth, and you&#39;re comfortable leaving lower-value work undone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decisive.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;d rather make a well-reasoned call today than a perfect one next month, and you&#39;re open about the assumptions behind it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical.&lt;/strong&gt; You break a problem down, work out what would need to be true, and go and find the data to test it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear and concise.&lt;/strong&gt; You write and present crisply, lead with the recommendation, and cut what the audience doesn&#39;t need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open on feedback.&lt;/strong&gt; You give it directly and kindly, ask for it, and act on it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A doer.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;d rather build a prototype and a short one-pager than write an extensive PRD about one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product experience within a complicated B2B data platform business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product experience within marketing or advertising technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits (UK)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A workplace pension, through Royal London, with Fospha matching your contributions up to 3%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A £1,000/year flexible benefits allowance to put towards private medical insurance, dental cover, a health cash plan, gym membership, extra holiday, or a pension top-up - whatever suits you!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to Wellhub, giving you one membership across gyms, boutique studios, and wellbeing apps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days&#39; annual leave plus 8 UK bank holidays, an extra day off for your birthday! and more holiday the longer you stay (26 days after 3 years, 27 after 6)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life assurance worth 4x your annual salary, from day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cycle to Work scheme, plus discounts on everyday spending through our benefits portal - Apple, Tesco, IKEA, M&amp;amp;S, Deliveroo, cinema tickets and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quarterly one-to-one sessions with a financial adviser, plus access to payroll-deducted loans through Salary Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid volunteering days each year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular socials, free weekly snacks, and Lunch &amp;amp; Learn events at our Scale Space office, plus access to the wider Blenheim Chalcot community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities to travel - including to our India and North America offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fin.ai/&quot;&gt;Fin&lt;/a&gt;, now part of Salesforce, is on a mission to help businesses provide perfect customer experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our AI Agent Fin is the highest-performing AI Customer Agent on the market today, enabling businesses to deliver impeccable, always-on customer support across the customer journey, from service, to sales, to ecommerce. Powered by our own AI models, Fin resolves complex customer issues end-to-end across every channel, with minimal set-up and integration. Fin can also be combined with our natively integrated Intercom help desk, giving modern support teams one single system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Together with Salesforce, the #1 AI CRM, where humans with agents drive customer success, we&#39;re building the future of customer experience. Here, ambition meets action. Tech meets trust. And innovation isn&#39;t a buzzword, it&#39;s a way of life. The world of work as we know it is changing, and we&#39;re looking for Trailblazers who are passionate about bettering business and the world through AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to level up your career at the company leading workforce transformation in the agentic era? You&#39;re in the right place. Agentforce is the future of AI, and you are the future of Salesforce.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;What&#39;s the opportunity?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Fin becomes mission-critical for our most strategic customers, we’re growing our team of Forward Deployed Engineers to help bridge the gap between customer needs and product innovation. This is a hybrid role, based in either our London or Dublin office.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer, you’ll work hands-on with strategic customers, partnering closely with our R&amp;amp;D and Go-to-Market teams to design and deliver high-impact solutions. You’ll go beyond implementation - helping shape product direction, influence roadmap decisions and ensure Fin delivers real, measurable business outcomes in complex, real-world environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re excited by ownership, creativity and solving ambiguous problems, and want to work at the frontier of applied AI while collaborating with Product, Engineering and Go-to-Market teams, this role offers a rare opportunity to combine technical excellence with real customer impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What will I be doing?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption of Fin by helping customers unlock the power of our AI capabilities to automate and scale their support operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed deeply with strategic customers to understand their business challenges and technical requirements, and provide the insight needed to achieve outstanding results with Fin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hands-on with customers’ technical teams as a trusted technical expert, coding side-by-side to drive projects through to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Sales, Success and Product teams to ensure seamless customer experiences, successful project delivery and actionable product feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the evolution of Forward Deployed Engineering by codifying best practices and sharing insights from customer engagements to help the team scale and grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What skills do I need?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong engineering background and experience building software with real-world usage. Experience building a SaaS product is a plus, but not a requirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in AI and machine learning, and the ability to quickly build an understanding of novel problems, capabilities and architectures - including their trade-offs and limitations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration skills, with the ability to navigate organisational boundaries and bring people together to achieve the best outcomes for our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of at least one high-level programming language, such as JavaScript, Python or Ruby. It doesn’t need to be a language we use today - great people learn quickly and can introduce us to better ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to prototype and ship software quickly while maintaining a high bar for quality and a clear focus on business goals and outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency using and writing REST APIs to integrate systems effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills. You can comfortably discuss the same topics with engineers and non-technical audiences, adapting the depth and detail as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel and work on-site with customers to build strong relationships and deeply understand their needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unleash Your Potential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you join Salesforce, you’ll be limitless in all areas of your life. Our benefits and resources support you to find balance and be your best, and our AI agents accelerate your impact so you can do your best. Together, we’ll bring the power of Agentforce to organizations of all sizes and deliver amazing experiences that customers love. Apply today to not only shape the future — but to redefine what’s possible — for yourself, for AI, and the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the United States, compensation offered will be determined by factors such as location, job level, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. Certain roles may be eligible for incentive compensation, equity, and benefits. At Fin, we want to give people what they need to do the best work of their careers. Our benefits and programs are designed to support your health and wellbeing, your family, your time away from work, and your financial future. Offerings vary by location in line with local practices and requirements. Learn more about working at Fin and the benefits we offer at&lt;a href=&quot;http://fin.ai/careers&quot;&gt; fin.ai/careers&lt;/a&gt;. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance and the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring, Salesforce will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Policies&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fin has a hybrid working policy. We believe that working in person helps us stay connected, collaborate easier and create a great culture while still providing flexibility to work from home. We expect employees to be in the office at least three days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a radically open and accepting culture at Fin. We avoid spending time on divisive subjects to foster a safe and cohesive work environment for everyone. As an organization, our policy is to not advocate on behalf of the company or our employees on any social or political topics out of our internal or external communications. We respect personal opinion and expression on these topics on personal social platforms on personal time, and do not challenge or confront anyone for their views on non-work related topics. Our goal is to focus on doing incredible work to achieve our goals and unite the company through our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.intercom.com/careers&quot;&gt;core values&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salesforce is an equal opportunity employer and maintains a policy of non-discrimination with all employees and applicants for employment. What does that mean exactly? It means that at Salesforce, we believe in equality for all. And we believe we can lead the path to equality in part by creating a workplace that’s inclusive, and free from discrimination.&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/know-your-rights-workplace-discrimination-illegal&quot;&gt;Know your rights: workplace discrimination is illegal.&lt;/a&gt; Any employee or potential employee will be assessed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications – without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender expression or identity, transgender status, age, disability, veteran or marital status, political viewpoint, or other classifications protected by law. This policy applies to current and prospective employees, no matter where they are in their Salesforce employment journey. It also applies to recruiting, hiring, job assignment, compensation, promotion, benefits, training, assessment of job performance, discipline, termination, and everything in between. Recruiting, hiring, and promotion decisions at Salesforce are fair and based on merit. The same goes for compensation, benefits, promotions, transfers, reduction in workforce, recall, training, and education.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ogilvy &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ogilvy has been creating impact for brands through iconic, culture-changing, value-driving ideas since the company was founded by David Ogilvy more than 75 years ago. It builds on that rich legacy through Borderless Creativity—innovating at the intersection of intelligence, imagination and influence, with experts across advertising, sports &amp;amp; entertainment, PR &amp;amp; social, consulting, and health collaborating seamlessly across more than 120 offices spanning 90 countries. Ogilvy was named &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ogilvy.com/ideas/ogilvy-brings-home-network-year-2026-cannes-lions-international-festival-creativity&quot;&gt;Network of the Year&lt;/a&gt; at the 2026 Cannes Lions International Festival of Creativity and&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ogilvy.com/ideas/ogilvy-tops-warc-effective-100-creative-100-4th-straight-year&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;e2c78315-ff05-4544-925f-9288319dea2c&quot;&gt;ranks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;as the #1 global agency network for creative excellence and effectiveness by WARC for the fourth consecutive year, signifying its ability to deliver creative solutions that drive unreasonable impact for clients and communities. Ogilvy is part of WPP, the trusted growth partner for the world&#39;s leading brands. Powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform WPP Open, WPP unites cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, creativity, production, enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ogilvy.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;39833259-880d-4fd8-930f-0d84b1c14850&quot;&gt;Ogilvy.com&lt;/a&gt;, and follow us on&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/ogilvy/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;735e393e-6e8a-4ca8-804a-74f1bd8166b6&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/ogilvy&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;d10960ce-761b-48c5-81d5-0a7c4cc6013a&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/ogilvy/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;92ffcb70-6ca7-4d9a-88d5-c130e36e6c4f&quot;&gt; Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/ogilvy/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;3bd2010d-00a2-401b-8cfb-7e8c24deac52&quot;&gt; Facebook.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WPP&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
